From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd: a task keeps its triggers, principal and actions

The Task Scheduler's object model lost most of a task on its way to the
service. Reading a definition's XML skipped its triggers and actions
(both readers were stubs), the principal's account, group and logon type
were stubs, a trigger made with ITriggerCollection::Create was never put
in the collection, Count and Item of both collections were stubs, and
writing a definition wrote no triggers and an empty Exec. A task
registered from XML went through that object model and was stored
without them: Microsoft Edge's update tasks were kept with no trigger and
an empty Exec, and an updater that builds its definition through the
object model (Chromium's) registered nothing that could ever run. Run,
LastRunTime, LastTaskResult, put_Enabled and Stop of a registered task
were stubs.

Now:
- triggers of their own (trigger.c): time, daily and weekly calendars,
  log-on, boot, registration and idle triggers with their properties and
  a repetition pattern each; the trigger collection keeps what Create
  makes, with Count, Item, Remove and Clear; they are read from and
  written to the task XML (TimeTrigger, CalendarTrigger with
  ScheduleByDay/ScheduleByWeek, LogonTrigger, BootTrigger,
  RegistrationTrigger, IdleTrigger, Repetition);
- the principal keeps its id, display name, user, group, logon type and
  run level, all read and written;
- the action collection keeps its actions and context; Exec actions are
  read and written (Command, Arguments, WorkingDirectory);
- MultipleInstancesPolicy's other values are read; text in the XML is
  written escaped (an argument with ">" or "&" made the XML malformed);
- RegisterTask hands the service the program's own XML (it is still read
  first to check it), so what the object model does not model is kept;
  RegisterTaskDefinition's user and logon type become the principal's,
  as on Windows;
- a registered task's Run and RunEx (the service runs it), LastRunTime,
  LastTaskResult, put_Enabled and Stop ask the service; Run gives an
  IRunningTask.

Test: test/taskrun-gate.sh with test/taskrun-probe.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_TASK_DROP_TRIGGERS, SG_MUTANT_TASK_REWRITE_XML; with patch
1172).
